name atomic-10x-tuples
# Every line is one object. Its members "head", "relation" and "tail" are the tuple, in that order, each as written:
# [head, relation, tail], which the set attests, scored by "p_valid_model", the number between 0 and 1 the line gives
# every tuple. "rec_0.5" .. "rec_0.9" are true or false on every line, and "split" is which part of the release a line
# is in; no documentation on this machine says what the rec_* members mean. Neither says anything of the tuple, and
# neither is read.
match ATOMIC10X.jsonl
format json
tier record by \n

thing record head relation tail
content head relation tail
omit split rec_* p_valid_model
itself record
score record p_valid_model
